ous purification of  monoclonal antibody products foreign  if you look at the current portfolio of  drugs that are provided by the  biopharmaceutical industry you see that  the best seller list is dominated by  monoclonal antibody and monoclonal  antibody related products like Fusion  proteins annual sales of monoclonal  antibodies are now greater than 100  billion dollars a year and there are  exciting New Opportunities some of you  may have studied the Press reports on  the release of monoclonal antibodies for  the treatment of Alzheimer's as well as  covid-19 these open up exciting new  avenues for the development of  Biotherapeutics  now if you look at the overview of the  manufacturing process for producing  monoclonal antibodies  um they all look generally the same  beginning with a bioreactor either  single use or stainless steel uh in the  case of antibodies typically used to  grow Chinese hamster ovary cells and  then you go through a series of steps  involving clarification primary capture  polishing and formulation  now the industry today accomplishes this  purification or a set of operations uh  in a fully batch mode that is each step  in the process is completed before the  next step is even begun so you would  grow your sales and uh they would  produce your product in the bioreactor  at the end of that process you would  clarify the entire suspension to remove  host cells and sell debris you would  then take that entire batch of material  and go through the primary capture step  and then subsequently through polishing  and formulation this typically requires  large stainless steel tanks uh the  standard bioreactor for monoclonal  antibody production is usually a 20 000  liter size reactor and it requires a  long period of time typically if you  look at the time going from the  beginning of the process to actually  having a formulated drug product it  averages about a hundred days  now this type of production process has  been recognized for many years 