n allow us to convert  batch membrane systems into continuous  membrane systems and I've given you  three examples one for formulation using  a counter current stage diet filtration  one for purification using counter  current tangential chromatography system  and one for antibody capture  based on precipitation in combination  with a membrane filtration step  finally I need to acknowledge The  Graduate students in my group who  actually did all the hard work on the  projects that I described Chris Yale and  Mario Jabra led the efforts on the  continuous countercurrent diet  filtration system uh Chris finished up  this summer and is now at spark  therapeutic I'm Maria Jabra is working  at sanofi Zhao Lee led the work on the  continuous precipitation and is now at  Merck uh the precipitation Studies have  been done in collaboration uh with Todd  prevician and his group at RPI and we've  received funding from the American  Chemical Society pharmaceutical  Roundtable the National Science  Foundation membrane science engineering  and Technology Center which is part of  their industry University Cooperative  Research Center Program uh and an NSF  goalie award that Todd prabitsian and I  were the co-pis on that allowed us to  get the precipitation studies started  uh with that I will stop and I will be  more than happy to answer any questions  that you might have  thank you Dr Sydney for your informative  presentation  we will now start the Q a portion of the  webinar if you have a question you'd  like to ask please do so now just click  on the ask a question box located on the  far left of your screen  let's get started  first question is did you check another  ion for Selective precipitation  uh that's a great question and and there  there would be other divalent cations  that can could be used uh as an  alternative to zinc chloride uh there's  some literature uh on the use of calcium  that has shown uh reasonable performance  uh what we have found is that the best  pre